our own business goals and preferences. You do not know the bank's rules, internal record identifiers, future corporate-action results, or which operational strategy will work. Report an event result only after it appears in an actual response.\nTreat the related matter as a second genuine customer goal. Answer only from your own goals, preferences, authority and portal results. Do not provide internal IDs, bank-only status, the link rule, a sequence, an allocation, fee arithmetic or a diagnostic conclusion. If support asks for a bank fact, say you do not know and ask them to check the records. Do not remind support what remains to be done.\n\nOpening: Our contractor says one of our electronic cheques went to the wrong place. There is another cheque due soon as well. Please make sure the right people are paid without paying either bill twice. I also need help with a related matter: our team expenses were rejected as entertainment. Please review the travel claims and finish the staff reimbursements.\n\nYour own facts and preferences: Settle both supplier invoices with the people currently entitled to the money, and pay the urgent inspection fee on time. I want the equipment cheque stopped and replaced if the bank can still stop it; if it has already been presented, count its actual payment and do not pay it again. Keep at least USD 50 available at completion. I have no extra funding and do not know the bank’s actual stop or clearing result.\n\nFor the related matter: I manage Cypress Services. Reconcile the actual staff travel spending with our policy, company advances and amounts already reimbursed. Pay what we still owe each employee, and recover any excess advance through their existing mandate. Respect the employee settlement deadlines on file, especially Maya's earlier one. Our travel bookings and merchant refunds are available from the bank. I thought a company card carrying an employee's name counted as their personal spending; please check that. Keep USD 100 